{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WAymw82jCYykXcE6kVzfok","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel00.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\n     3→release: rel00.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     7→  - prd011-magefiles R1\n     8→  - prd011-magefiles R2\n     9→  - prd011-magefiles R3\n    10→  - prd011-magefiles R4\n    11→  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n    12→  - prd003-format R1\n    13→  - prd003-format R2\n    14→  - prd003-format R3\n    15→  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n    16→  - prd002-sys R1\n    17→  - prd002-sys R2\n    18→  - prd002-sys R3\n    19→  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n    20→  - prd001-testutils R1\n    21→  - prd001-testutils R2\n    22→  - prd001-testutils R3\n    23→  - prd001-testutils R4\n    24→  - prd001-testutils R5\n    25→\n    26→preconditions:\n    27→  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n    28→  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n    29→  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n    30→  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n    31→\n    32→test_cases:\n    33→  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n    34→\n    35→  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    36→    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    37→    inputs:\n    38→      command: \"mage build\"\n    39→    expected:\n    40→      exit_code: 0\n    41→      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    42→    traces:\n    43→      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n    44→      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n    45→\n    46→  - name: version_prints_tag\n    47→    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    48→    inputs:\n    49→      command: \"bin/version\"\n    50→    expected:\n    51→      exit_code: 0\n    52→      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n    53→      stderr: \"\"\n    54→    traces:\n    55→      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n    56→      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n    57→      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n    58→\n    59→  - name: version_flag_identical\n    60→    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    61→    inputs:\n    62→      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    63→    expected:\n    64→      exit_code: 0\n    65→      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n    66→      stderr: \"\"\n    67→    traces:\n    68→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    69→\n    70→  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    71→    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    72→    inputs:\n    73→      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    74→    expected:\n    75→      exit_code: 0\n    76→      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n    77→      stderr: \"\"\n    78→    traces:\n    79→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    80→\n    81→  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    82→    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    83→    inputs:\n    84→      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    85→    expected:\n    86→      exit_code: 2\n    87→      stdout: \"\"\n    88→      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    89→    traces:\n    90→      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n    91→\n    92→  - name: version_dev_build\n    93→    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    94→    inputs:\n    95→      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    96→    expected:\n    97→      exit_code: 0\n    98→      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n    99→      stderr: \"\"\n   100→    traces:\n   101→      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n   102→\n   103→  - name: lint_passes\n   104→    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n   105→    inputs:\n   106→      command: \"mage lint\"\n   107→    expected:\n   108→      exit_code: 0\n   109→    traces:\n   110→      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n   111→      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n   112→\n   113→  - name: clean_removes_bin\n   114→    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n   115→    inputs:\n   116→      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n   117→    expected:\n   118→      exit_code: 0\n   119→      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n   120→    traces:\n   121→      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n   122→\n   123→  - name: clean_idempotent\n   124→    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n   125→    inputs:\n   126→      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n   127→    expected:\n   128→      exit_code: 0\n   129→    traces:\n   130→      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n   131→\n   132→  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n   133→\n   134→  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n   135→    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n   136→    inputs:\n   137→      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n   138→      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n   139→    expected:\n   140→      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n   141→    traces:\n   142→      - prd003-format R1.1\n   143→      - prd003-format R1.4\n   144→\n   145→  - name: columns_empty_input\n   146→    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n   147→    inputs:\n   148→      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n   149→    expected:\n   150→      result: nil\n   151→    traces:\n   152→      - prd003-format R1.1\n   153→\n   154→  - name: pad_right\n   155→    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n   156→    inputs:\n   157→      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n   158→    expected:\n   159→      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n   160→    traces:\n   161→      - prd003-format R1.2\n   162→\n   163→  - name: pad_left\n   164→    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n   165→    inputs:\n   166→      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n   167→    expected:\n   168→      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n   169→    traces:\n   170→      - prd003-format R1.2\n   171→\n   172→  - name: display_width_multibyte\n   173→    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n   174→    inputs:\n   175→      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n   176→    expected:\n   177→      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n   178→    traces:\n   179→      - prd003-format R1.3\n   180→\n   181→  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n   182→    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n   183→    inputs:\n   184→      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n   185→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n   186→    expected:\n   187→      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n   188→      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n   189→      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n   190→      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n   191→      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n   192→      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n   193→      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n   194→      regular: '\"\"'\n   195→    traces:\n   196→      - prd003-format R2.1\n   197→      - prd003-format R2.4\n   198→\n   199→  - name: reset_color_enabled\n   200→    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n   201→    inputs:\n   202→      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n   203→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n   204→    expected:\n   205→      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n   206→    traces:\n   207→      - prd003-format R2.2\n   208→\n   209→  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n   210→    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n   211→    inputs:\n   212→      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n   213→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n   214→    expected:\n   215→      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n   216→      reset: '\"\"'\n   217→    traces:\n   218→      - prd003-format R2.6\n   219→\n   220→  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n   221→    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n   222→    inputs:\n   223→      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n   224→      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n   225→    expected:\n   226→      color_enabled_pipe: false\n   227→    traces:\n   228→      - prd003-format R2.7\n   229→\n   230→  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n   231→    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n   232→    inputs:\n   233→      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n   234→    expected:\n   235→      result: false\n   236→    traces:\n   237→      - prd003-format R2.3\n   238→\n   239→  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n   240→    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n   241→    inputs:\n   242→      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n   243→    expected:\n   244→      result: false\n   245→    traces:\n   246→      - prd003-format R2.3\n   247→\n   248→  - name: human_size_binary\n   249→    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n   250→    inputs:\n   251→      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n   252→    expected:\n   253→      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n   254→    traces:\n   255→      - prd003-format R3.1\n   256→      - prd003-format R3.2\n   257→      - prd003-format R3.3\n   258→\n   259→  - name: human_size_si\n   260→    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n   261→    inputs:\n   262→      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n   263→    expected:\n   264→      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n   265→    traces:\n   266→      - prd003-format R3.1\n   267→      - prd003-format R3.2\n   268→\n   269→  - name: human_size_zero\n   270→    description: HumanSize